--- a/docs/specs/session.md
+++ b/docs/specs/session.md
@@ -83,3 +83,5 @@ host), covering spec tests 1 to 3 against the real session (P6 extends this to a
 - **Hub address:** the app sets `window.__ORLIS_PAD_HUB__ = { port, key, lan? }` (`lan`: this computer's address on the home network, for the QR; or `url`).
   Browser dev (owner or dev server only): `?padhub=<port>:<key>` and optional `&padhost=<lan address>` point at `node tools/pad-hub.mjs`.
 - Added to the session: `canStart` (true when `start()` would work). Pad programs live in `app/pads/<game>/pad.js` (the Node hub serves that folder at `/pads/`).
+- **Optional phones (S2, Opus review 2026-11-22):** a game whose manifest has `seats.pads[0] === 0` (Pop Party) **never shows the join card**. The round starts as it always did (the shell sets the tracked seats and calls `session.start()` itself), and phones drop in at any time: a phone that joins mid-round gets its game object at once (`pads.on('join')`), and trusted phones rejoin by themselves. While the hub is running the shell shows a **join chip** during play: the QR and the three pictures, bottom-right, about 15% of the screen height, semi-transparent (`app/src/ui/join-chip.js`); it hides once every pad seat is taken (`rt.full`) and comes back if one frees up. The pause screen shows the same QR and pictures, larger. Games that need a phone (`pads[0] > 0`: pad-lab, later Peekaboo) keep the join card.
+- **Phones count as present:** `rt.activeSeats(secs)` lists the pad seats heard from in the last `secs` seconds. The shell's "nobody in view" overlay does not show while any pad seat has been heard in the last 10 s, and pad players that have sent input are in the shell's `joined` set (so in the best-score player count).
